Negative control for contract-product.i18n-keys.int.test.ts (FE-3029, D87).

Assertion it attacks: every two-position toggle the list-page filter bar lays
out labels each position from `<control.i18n>.<enum value>`, and that key must
resolve to real copy in `packages/i18n/src/core/form-en.json` — never a raw key
a renderer would draw on screen (`form.contract_product_one_time_only.0`). The
test derives the positions off the module's LIVE published schema, from the
`billing_cycle_days` operator leaves' own `enum` members.

The mutation: the one-time-only toggle's `eq` leaf offers the enum member `9`
in place of `0`. The catalogue carries `form.contract_product_one_time_only.0`
("One-time only") and `.null` ("All") but no `.9`, so the derived position
`form.contract_product_one_time_only.9` resolves to nothing and its case goes
red. The control's own label and its `.null` position still resolve — which is
what makes this a control on the POSITION-copy check, not a broad breakage.

